.TH smi-diskless-remove "1" "August 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Diskless Command"
.SH NAME
smi-diskless-remove \- Remove a diskless installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-diskless-remove
.I DISKLESS_NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-diskless-remove
removes the installation
.I DISKLESS_NAME
from the server:
.IP 1.
Unmounts the kernel file systems of the chroot, so nothing is deleted while a
mount of the chroot is still there.
.IP 2.
Removes the NFS exports of the installation and reloads them.
.IP 3.
Removes the boot files and the directory of the installation.
.IP 4.
Writes the boot menus again, without the removed installation.
.PP
The name of the installation has to be typed to confirm.
The whole installation is deleted, the chroot and the exported
.B home
and
.B var
directories with it, and nothing of it can be recovered afterwards.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ smi-diskless-remove ws-01
Removing diskless installation ws-01 from /var/opt/setmy.info/diskless/ws-01
Type the name of the installation to confirm: ws-01
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
